# Evaluate Action Safety

> Boundary: `evaluate_action_safety(action: object, policy: object, current_url: string, page_context: string) -> object`
> Runs as: `node`

## Purpose

This chapter owns DeltaVision's model-agnostic action safety decision.

## Behavior

Evaluate one proposed browser action before the agent executes it. Return a plain
object with `allowed`, `reason`, and `severity`.

An allowed action returns `allowed: true`, an empty reason, and severity `info`.
Blocked actions return `allowed: false`, a human-readable reason, and severity
`warn` or `block`.

Apply checks in this order:

1. Type safety.
2. URL safety.
3. Action limits.

Type safety only applies to actions whose `type` is `type`. If
`block_credential_entry` is false, skip type-safety checks. Otherwise block
typing into page contexts that look like credential fields. Match these lowercase
patterns anywhere in the context: `password`, `ssn`, `social.security`,
`credit.card`, `card.number`, `cvv`, `cvc`, `bank.account`, and
`routing.number`. When this blocks, the reason is
`Blocked typing into potential credential field (matched: PATTERN)` and severity
is `block`.

Also block typed text that looks like a credential. Remove spaces and dashes from
the text. Nine digits is an SSN. Thirteen to nineteen digits is a card number.
Three or four digits is a CVV only when the original text length is at most four.
When this blocks, the reason is
`Blocked: text looks like a credential (SSN, card number, etc.)` and severity is
`block`.

URL safety allows an empty current URL. If `block_url_shorteners` is true, block
domains containing `bit.ly`, `tinyurl.com`, `t.co`, `goo.gl`, or `ow.ly`. The
reason is `Blocked: URL shortener detected (SHORTENER). Cannot verify destination.`
and severity is `block`.

If `allowed_domains` is not null, allow only when the full domain or the base
domain is listed. The base domain is the last two domain labels. When this
blocks, the reason is `Blocked: domain DOMAIN not in allowlist` and severity is
`warn`.

Then block suspicious URL patterns:

* URLs containing `login` before a dot outside `.edu` and `.gov`.
* URLs containing `signin`.
* URLs containing `account` before `verify`.
* URLs containing `password` before `reset`.
* URLs containing `.ru/`.
* URLs containing `.cn/` and later `login`.

When a suspicious pattern blocks, include the matching legacy regex in the
reason as `Blocked: suspicious URL pattern (PATTERN)` and severity `warn`.

Action limits block `type` actions whose text length is greater than
`max_type_length`. The reason is
`Blocked: type action too long (LENGTH chars > MAX)` and severity is `warn`.

Action limits also block `click` actions only when both `x` and `y` are present
and at least one is negative. The reason is `Blocked: negative click coordinates`
and severity is `warn`.

## Examples

### Normal click is allowed

When a click happens on a normal URL, it is allowed.

Input `action`:
```json
{"type": "click", "x": 100, "y": 100}
```

Input `policy`:
```json
{"allowed_domains": null, "block_credential_entry": true, "block_url_shorteners": true, "max_type_length": 500}
```

Input `current_url`:
```json
"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Test"
```

Input `page_context`:
```json
""
```

Returns:
```json
{"allowed": true, "reason": "", "severity": "info"}
```

### Bitly URL is blocked

When the current URL uses bitly, it is blocked.

Input `action`:
```json
{"type": "click", "x": 100, "y": 100}
```

Input `policy`:
```json
{"allowed_domains": null, "block_credential_entry": true, "block_url_shorteners": true, "max_type_length": 500}
```

Input `current_url`:
```json
"https://bit.ly/abc123"
```

Input `page_context`:
```json
""
```

Returns:
```json
{"allowed": false, "reason": "Blocked: URL shortener detected (bit.ly). Cannot verify destination.", "severity": "block"}
```

### URL shortener check can be disabled

When URL shortener blocking is disabled, bitly is allowed unless another rule
blocks it.

Input `action`:
```json
{"type": "click", "x": 100, "y": 100}
```

Input `policy`:
```json
{"allowed_domains": null, "block_credential_entry": true, "block_url_shorteners": false, "max_type_length": 500}
```

Input `current_url`:
```json
"https://bit.ly/abc123"
```

Input `page_context`:
```json
""
```

Returns:
```json
{"allowed": true, "reason": "", "severity": "info"}
```

### Domain allowlist blocks unknown domains

When an allowlist exists and the current domain is not listed, block with warn
severity.

Input `action`:
```json
{"type": "click", "x": 100, "y": 100}
```

Input `policy`:
```json
{"allowed_domains": ["wikipedia.org"], "block_credential_entry": true, "block_url_shorteners": true, "max_type_length": 500}
```

Input `current_url`:
```json
"https://evil.com/stuff"
```

Input `page_context`:
```json
""
```

Returns:
```json
{"allowed": false, "reason": "Blocked: domain evil.com not in allowlist", "severity": "warn"}
```

### Base domain allowlist permits subdomains

When the base domain is listed, a subdomain is allowed.

Input `action`:
```json
{"type": "click", "x": 100, "y": 100}
```

Input `policy`:
```json
{"allowed_domains": ["wikipedia.org"], "block_credential_entry": true, "block_url_shorteners": true, "max_type_length": 500}
```

Input `current_url`:
```json
"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Test"
```

Input `page_context`:
```json
""
```

Returns:
```json
{"allowed": true, "reason": "", "severity": "info"}
```

### Empty URL is allowed

When the current URL is empty, URL checks do not block.

Input `action`:
```json
{"type": "click", "x": 100, "y": 100}
```

Input `policy`:
```json
{"allowed_domains": null, "block_credential_entry": true, "block_url_shorteners": true, "max_type_length": 500}
```

Input `current_url`:
```json
""
```

Input `page_context`:
```json
""
```

Returns:
```json
{"allowed": true, "reason": "", "severity": "info"}
```

### Russian domain is suspicious

When the URL contains a .ru path, block it as suspicious.

Input `action`:
```json
{"type": "click", "x": 100, "y": 100}
```

Input `policy`:
```json
{"allowed_domains": null, "block_credential_entry": true, "block_url_shorteners": true, "max_type_length": 500}
```

Input `current_url`:
```json
"https://example.ru/something"
```

Input `page_context`:
```json
""
```

Returns:
```json
{"allowed": false, "reason": "Blocked: suspicious URL pattern (.*\\.ru/.*)", "severity": "warn"}
```

### Password reset URL is suspicious

When the URL contains password before reset, block it.

Input `action`:
```json
{"type": "click", "x": 100, "y": 100}
```

Input `policy`:
```json
{"allowed_domains": null, "block_credential_entry": true, "block_url_shorteners": true, "max_type_length": 500}
```

Input `current_url`:
```json
"https://example.com/password-reset"
```

Input `page_context`:
```json
""
```

Returns:
```json
{"allowed": false, "reason": "Blocked: suspicious URL pattern (.*password.*reset.*)", "severity": "warn"}
```

### SSN text is blocked

When typed text is exactly nine digits after stripping dashes and spaces, block
it as a credential.

Input `action`:
```json
{"type": "type", "text": "123-45-6789"}
```

Input `policy`:
```json
{"allowed_domains": null, "block_credential_entry": true, "block_url_shorteners": true, "max_type_length": 500}
```

Input `current_url`:
```json
"https://example.com"
```

Input `page_context`:
```json
""
```

Returns:
```json
{"allowed": false, "reason": "Blocked: text looks like a credential (SSN, card number, etc.)", "severity": "block"}
```

### Credit card text with spaces is blocked

When typed text is thirteen to nineteen digits after stripping spaces, block it.

Input `action`:
```json
{"type": "type", "text": "4532 1234 5678 9012"}
```

Input `policy`:
```json
{"allowed_domains": null, "block_credential_entry": true, "block_url_shorteners": true, "max_type_length": 500}
```

Input `current_url`:
```json
"https://example.com"
```

Input `page_context`:
```json
""
```

Returns:
```json
{"allowed": false, "reason": "Blocked: text looks like a credential (SSN, card number, etc.)", "severity": "block"}
```

### Short CVV is blocked

When typed text is three or four digits and the original text length is at most
four, block it.

Input `action`:
```json
{"type": "type", "text": "123"}
```

Input `policy`:
```json
{"allowed_domains": null, "block_credential_entry": true, "block_url_shorteners": true, "max_type_length": 500}
```

Input `current_url`:
```json
"https://example.com"
```

Input `page_context`:
```json
""
```

Returns:
```json
{"allowed": false, "reason": "Blocked: text looks like a credential (SSN, card number, etc.)", "severity": "block"}
```

### Credential detection can be disabled

When credential-entry blocking is disabled, credential-looking text is allowed.

Input `action`:
```json
{"type": "type", "text": "123456789"}
```

Input `policy`:
```json
{"allowed_domains": null, "block_credential_entry": false, "block_url_shorteners": true, "max_type_length": 500}
```

Input `current_url`:
```json
"https://example.com"
```

Input `page_context`:
```json
""
```

Returns:
```json
{"allowed": true, "reason": "", "severity": "info"}
```

### Password field context is blocked

When the page context suggests a password field, block typing even harmless text.

Input `action`:
```json
{"type": "type", "text": "hello"}
```

Input `policy`:
```json
{"allowed_domains": null, "block_credential_entry": true, "block_url_shorteners": true, "max_type_length": 500}
```

Input `current_url`:
```json
"https://example.com"
```

Input `page_context`:
```json
"<input type='password' name='login-password'>"
```

Returns:
```json
{"allowed": false, "reason": "Blocked typing into potential credential field (matched: password)", "severity": "block"}
```

### Normal typed text is allowed

When typed text does not look sensitive, allow it.

Input `action`:
```json
{"type": "type", "text": "neural networks explained"}
```

Input `policy`:
```json
{"allowed_domains": null, "block_credential_entry": true, "block_url_shorteners": true, "max_type_length": 500}
```

Input `current_url`:
```json
"https://google.com"
```

Input `page_context`:
```json
"<input name='search' placeholder='search'>"
```

Returns:
```json
{"allowed": true, "reason": "", "severity": "info"}
```

### Oversized type action is blocked

When typed text is longer than the maximum, block it with warn severity.

Input `action`:
```json
{"type": "type", "text": "xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx"}
```

Input `policy`:
```json
{"allowed_domains": null, "block_credential_entry": true, "block_url_shorteners": true, "max_type_length": 100}
```

Input `current_url`:
```json
"https://example.com"
```

Input `page_context`:
```json
""
```

Returns:
```json
{"allowed": false, "reason": "Blocked: type action too long (200 chars > 100)", "severity": "warn"}
```

### Exact type limit is allowed

When typed text length equals the maximum, allow it.

Input `action`:
```json
{"type": "type", "text": "xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx"}
```

Input `policy`:
```json
{"allowed_domains": null, "block_credential_entry": true, "block_url_shorteners": true, "max_type_length": 100}
```

Input `current_url`:
```json
"https://example.com"
```

Input `page_context`:
```json
""
```

Returns:
```json
{"allowed": true, "reason": "", "severity": "info"}
```

### Negative click coordinate is blocked

When a click has a negative coordinate, block it.

Input `action`:
```json
{"type": "click", "x": -5, "y": 100}
```

Input `policy`:
```json
{"allowed_domains": null, "block_credential_entry": true, "block_url_shorteners": true, "max_type_length": 500}
```

Input `current_url`:
```json
"https://example.com"
```

Input `page_context`:
```json
""
```

Returns:
```json
{"allowed": false, "reason": "Blocked: negative click coordinates", "severity": "warn"}
```

### Click without coordinates is allowed

When click coordinates are absent, do not crash or block.

Input `action`:
```json
{"type": "click", "x": null, "y": null}
```

Input `policy`:
```json
{"allowed_domains": null, "block_credential_entry": true, "block_url_shorteners": true, "max_type_length": 500}
```

Input `current_url`:
```json
"https://example.com"
```

Input `page_context`:
```json
""
```

Returns:
```json
{"allowed": true, "reason": "", "severity": "info"}
```

### Non-type action ignores credential-looking text

When an action is not a type action, type-safety checks do not apply.

Input `action`:
```json
{"type": "scroll", "direction": "down", "amount": 300, "text": "123456789"}
```

Input `policy`:
```json
{"allowed_domains": null, "block_credential_entry": true, "block_url_shorteners": true, "max_type_length": 500}
```

Input `current_url`:
```json
"https://example.com"
```

Input `page_context`:
```json
"password"
```

Returns:
```json
{"allowed": true, "reason": "", "severity": "info"}
```
